Time To Live (TTL) Analysis

Two different TTL values were observed.

TTL = 128

A TTL value of 128 is commonly associated with Microsoft Windows operating systems.

This suggests that one of the communicating systems may be a Windows host.

TTL = 232

A TTL value of 232 suggests that the originating device may have used an initial TTL of 255.

Estimated hop count

255 − 232 = 23 hops

This TTL value is commonly observed from routers, networking devices, and some Unix/Linux systems using an initial TTL of 255.

TTL values alone cannot accurately determine the operating system and should only be treated as an indicator rather than confirmation.

